    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "What can a processor prepare for withdrawn file closure?",
        "a": "A processor can organize approved source records, compare versions, maintain the exception state, and route evidence for review. The role does not decide eligibility, compliance, credit, valuation, legal effect, or approval."
      },
      {
        "q": "What should stop the workflow?",
        "a": "Stop when identity, authority, policy version, source evidence, privacy scope, or the accountable owner is unclear. Preserve the observed state and use the approved escalation route."
      },
      {
        "q": "What proves completion?",
        "a": "Completion requires a durable evidence link, a reviewable status history, the accountable owner's disposition, any approved communication evidence, and an explicit retention or reopening rule."
      }
    ],
